1
00:00:02,401 --> 00:00:06,772
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:16,081 --> 00:00:21,920
Okay, I'm not too sure what's going on
here, but that guy dropped his gun.

3
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:25,591
And guns open up a
wide world of opportunities.

4
00:00:25,591 --> 00:00:28,560
It has blood on it, but it's a glock...

5
00:00:28,927 --> 00:00:30,028
Blehk!

6
00:00:30,062 --> 00:00:31,663
As for you.

7
00:00:31,663 --> 00:00:32,865
Yeah...

8
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:36,869
Sweet!

9
00:00:36,869 --> 00:00:38,670
I want more things to shoot!

10
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:41,273
Besides this pile of rancid meat.

11
00:00:41,273 --> 00:00:42,307
Oh, that'll work.

12
00:00:43,175 --> 00:00:46,211
Okay, I don't think I've
fired a gun before

13
00:00:46,211 --> 00:00:49,681
but shooting things feels very familiar.

14
00:00:49,681 --> 00:00:52,885
And I didn't even have that dream
where I was Snoop Dogg again.

15
00:00:52,885 --> 00:00:56,221
Yeah, I don't know, I think
I shot somebody last night.

16
00:00:56,221 --> 00:00:57,923
Maybe a bunch of people.

17
00:00:57,923 --> 00:00:59,925
Well, I'm sure they had it coming.

18
00:00:59,925 --> 00:01:04,129
But, if that's true, I may have screwed
up WAY more than usual this time.

19
00:01:04,129 --> 00:01:05,497
I should watch my back.

20
00:01:05,497 --> 00:01:07,933
And what the hell are these things?

21
00:01:09,401 --> 00:01:10,769
Besides dead?

22
00:01:10,769 --> 00:01:12,871
Hm, I'm low on theories.

23
00:01:12,871 --> 00:01:16,208
I think maybe these are some
carnivorous plant cross-breeds that

24
00:01:16,208 --> 00:01:20,212
the Biology Department was working on
where the containment obviously failed.

25
00:01:20,212 --> 00:01:22,080
Kind of like Little Shop of Horrors.

26
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:25,117
Except we're the Big Shop of Horrors!

27
00:01:25,117 --> 00:01:27,853
Okay, I am still lost.

28
00:01:27,853 --> 00:01:29,521
Well, I think that's making sense.

29
00:01:29,521 --> 00:01:31,123
Biology had an accident,

30
00:01:31,123 --> 00:01:32,991
the specimen spread,

31
00:01:32,991 --> 00:01:35,327
but how do I play into this?

32
00:01:35,327 --> 00:01:38,630
I was probably down there trying to
hit on Heather again and

33
00:01:38,630 --> 00:01:41,266
maybe she just lost it and
knocked me unconscious

34
00:01:41,266 --> 00:01:45,971
Then tried to dump my body because,
let's face it, she's pretty stone cold.

35
00:01:45,971 --> 00:01:47,573
Shit, they're back.

36
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:52,878
Well, it didn't work, Heather!

37
00:01:52,878 --> 00:01:54,980
Now I have a gun!

38
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,915
You can't stop the Freeman!

39
00:01:56,915 --> 00:01:58,050
[lock jiggles]

40
00:01:58,050 --> 00:02:03,322
Well, okay, I guess doors
can stop the Freeman, but

41
00:02:03,322 --> 00:02:04,122
[lock jiggles]

42
00:02:04,122 --> 00:02:04,823
Damn.

43
00:02:05,223 --> 00:02:08,026
This kind of takes all the
wind out of my image.

44
00:02:08,026 --> 00:02:12,097
Actually, I don't know if
this was the Biology Department...

45
00:02:12,097 --> 00:02:14,800
Because, whatever those
things are, they're animals.

46
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,703
And we don't do a lot of
engineering with animals.

47
00:02:17,703 --> 00:02:19,738
There's just not enough money in it.

48
00:02:19,738 --> 00:02:22,007
Wait, I'm going backwards.

49
00:02:22,007 --> 00:02:22,975
I don't know.

50
00:02:22,975 --> 00:02:25,844
I mean, there was that pollen
we developed for Monsanto

51
00:02:25,844 --> 00:02:27,312
that would kill people.

52
00:02:27,312 --> 00:02:29,781
Everybody was really proud of that.

53
00:02:29,781 --> 00:02:30,782
I'm going to go out this way.

54
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:34,019
Squeeze in here...

55
00:02:35,721 --> 00:02:36,788
Whoa-whoa!

56
00:02:36,788 --> 00:02:38,857
Augh....

57
00:02:38,857 --> 00:02:42,661
Goat cheese massacre!
That hurts my knees!

58
00:02:42,661 --> 00:02:45,430
This suit needs shock absorbers.

59
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:46,999
And drugs.

60
00:02:46,999 --> 00:02:49,234
Why am I wearing this suit anyway?

61
00:02:49,234 --> 00:02:50,535
Did I steal it?

62
00:02:50,535 --> 00:02:53,405
I don't think I would've
been THAT stupid.

63
00:02:53,405 --> 00:02:57,709
If Black Mesa reported it stolen,
somehow I think the police would know

64
00:02:57,709 --> 00:03:00,812
to look for the last person
who was wearing it.

65
00:03:00,812 --> 00:03:02,948
I couldn't have been trying to steal it.

66
00:03:02,948 --> 00:03:05,350
Why, this must be--!  Yeah, I'm lost.

67
00:03:06,284 --> 00:03:09,655
So, if I'm wearing this suit,
that must mean we had an experiment.

68
00:03:09,655 --> 00:03:13,058
Hey, we did do the
experiment! I remember.

69
00:03:13,058 --> 00:03:14,426
...sort of...

70
00:03:14,426 --> 00:03:16,628
There was lots of green.

71
00:03:16,628 --> 00:03:20,766
Okay, so we had the experiment.
Then what happened?

72
00:03:20,766 --> 00:03:21,733
Oh, I know!

73
00:03:21,733 --> 00:03:24,302
Then I had to kill a
bunch of COCKROACHES!

74
00:03:24,302 --> 00:03:25,871
Because I HATE THEM!

75
00:03:25,871 --> 00:03:28,040
...want them all to DIE!  STOP!

76
00:03:29,174 --> 00:03:30,542
Then, after that...

77
00:03:30,542 --> 00:03:31,510
[lock jiggles]

78
00:03:31,510 --> 00:03:33,845
I got depressed...

79
00:03:33,845 --> 00:03:37,482
And...okay, this is easy to figure out.

80
00:03:37,482 --> 00:03:41,253
Because, if the experiment was a success,
I would've partied all night

81
00:03:41,253 --> 00:03:45,090
And got drunk off my ass and
probably woke up in a Dumpster. But!

82
00:03:45,357 --> 00:03:48,260
I woke up sober and that sucks.

83
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:51,530
So, that must mean the
experiment was NOT a success.

84
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:53,699
I probably got into some fights, then.

85
00:03:53,699 --> 00:03:56,401
Oh, man!  This is where I just was!

86
00:03:56,401 --> 00:03:58,537
Ah well, it beats the desert.

87
00:03:58,537 --> 00:04:00,605
Plus, I have a gun!

88
00:04:00,605 --> 00:04:02,808
So, my prosperity is assured.

89
00:04:02,808 --> 00:04:05,544
Now, I just have to find someone
and tell them I'm lost.

90
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:08,246
If they laugh at me
I point my gun at them.

91
00:04:08,246 --> 00:04:11,550
If they tell me they're too busy to talk
I point my gun at them.

92
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:13,285
It's really that simple.

93
00:04:13,285 --> 00:04:16,621
Okay, I don't think I've tried
this giant pot-stirring room.

94
00:04:16,621 --> 00:04:18,223
I'm not sure what they're stirring,

95
00:04:18,223 --> 00:04:22,694
but I'm guessing anything luminescent
and neon-green isn't very tasty.

96
00:04:22,694 --> 00:04:26,531
Okay, now if I hang down
properly, this should work.

97
00:04:28,433 --> 00:04:30,235
Ah, much better.

98
00:04:30,235 --> 00:04:32,270
Now, I just need to learn to do that faster

99
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:35,207
so I'll be ready when I come to work
with the smoke bombs.

100
00:04:35,207 --> 00:04:36,842
Wait, which way is north?

101
00:04:36,842 --> 00:04:38,243
You're not north.

102
00:04:38,243 --> 00:04:40,178
But.... no....

103
00:04:40,178 --> 00:04:41,847
Everyone here's a liar.

104
00:04:41,847 --> 00:04:43,448
I don't like liars.

105
00:04:43,448 --> 00:04:45,383
Christ, where am I?!

106
00:04:45,383 --> 00:04:48,920
This is just some
chemical processing facility.

107
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:53,959
I don't remember what I was planning to
do today, but I'm sure this isn't it.

108
00:04:53,959 --> 00:04:57,028
Black Mesa is NOT a tourist trap.

109
00:04:57,062 --> 00:04:59,965
Of course! I've already been here.

110
00:04:59,965 --> 00:05:03,602
It's not just me! NO ONE should be here.

111
00:05:03,602 --> 00:05:07,439
No one comes to a half-abandoned
warehouse unless they work there

112
00:05:07,439 --> 00:05:09,875
they're trying to film
a low-budget horror movie,

113
00:05:09,875 --> 00:05:13,278
or they're a photographer taking
bullshit black-and-white photos

114
00:05:13,278 --> 00:05:14,813
pretending to be artsy.

115
00:05:14,813 --> 00:05:15,814
That's it.

116
00:05:15,814 --> 00:05:18,450
And I'm going the wrong way again!

117
00:05:18,450 --> 00:05:21,887
I supposed I shouldn't expect the red
carpet treatment breaking and entering

118
00:05:21,887 --> 00:05:24,823
into to the site of a chemical plant,
but I still find the building layout

119
00:05:24,823 --> 00:05:27,459
confusing and I'll lodge a complaint
with the administration

120
00:05:27,459 --> 00:05:29,461
if I find the front desk.

121
00:05:30,162 --> 00:05:31,630
Well, not this way.

122
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:34,399
Oh, and I would also
like to file a complaint

123
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,268
about the number of locked doors here

124
00:05:36,268 --> 00:05:39,404
and about the mutant animals
that appear to be eating people.

125
00:05:40,172 --> 00:05:42,474
Trespasser or not, I have rights

126
00:05:42,474 --> 00:05:46,144
and I'm entitled to a reasonable
expectation of safety and comfort

127
00:05:46,144 --> 00:05:47,779
when I break into a place.

128
00:05:47,779 --> 00:05:50,282
This is America, after all!

129
00:05:50,282 --> 00:05:51,817
I need to get an attorney.

130
00:05:51,817 --> 00:05:56,388
This whole situation is completely
unreasonable for someone of my stature.

131
00:05:56,388 --> 00:05:57,522
And there is--

132
00:05:58,290 --> 00:06:00,892
Jesus Christ, this is the wrong way, too!

133
00:06:00,892 --> 00:06:03,829
Alright, I'm going to have to start
thinking outside the box here.

134
00:06:03,829 --> 00:06:07,199
I should think less like a
human being that uses doors

135
00:06:07,232 --> 00:06:11,002
and more like a squirrel
that has anger problems.

136
00:06:11,002 --> 00:06:13,004
Besides, I think it's entirely possible

137
00:06:13,004 --> 00:06:15,473
I'm the first person
to ever set foot here.

138
00:06:15,473 --> 00:06:17,409
My name will be in history books.

139
00:06:17,976 --> 00:06:22,447
Therefore, as these are new territories
discovered by the Nation of Freeman

140
00:06:22,447 --> 00:06:25,984
any and all claims shall henceforth
be named after me.

141
00:06:25,984 --> 00:06:26,952
Me!

142
00:06:26,952 --> 00:06:30,789
The official name of this
monument will be...the...

143
00:06:30,789 --> 00:06:36,895
Freeman Industrial-Strength Mixer
With Green Crap Inside of It.

144
00:06:37,796 --> 00:06:40,332
Hey, I think that's an
entrance over there.

145
00:06:40,332 --> 00:06:43,235
That seems entirely worth the risk.

146
00:06:43,235 --> 00:06:47,839
Especially since I really
don't know the contents of this.

147
00:06:48,406 --> 00:06:52,344
I mean, there's the
possibility that this really is

148
00:06:52,344 --> 00:06:56,615
just a giant vat of gelatin and dye

149
00:06:56,615 --> 00:06:59,918
even though it doesn't smell like it...

150
00:07:00,952 --> 00:07:03,288
I mean, this is normal,
what I'm doing, right?

151
00:07:03,288 --> 00:07:06,625
People do things like this all the time
when they get locked out of their office.

152
00:07:06,625 --> 00:07:10,195
And.... Oh, wow.
That thing could take my head off.

153
00:07:10,996 --> 00:07:12,631
Errragh!

154
00:07:12,631 --> 00:07:14,966
See, this is how you get promoted.

155
00:07:14,966 --> 00:07:17,802
What I'm doing right now, this
is progress.

156
00:07:17,802 --> 00:07:20,372
I'm...sure of it....

157
00:07:23,241 --> 00:07:27,245
Eh, if this ends up being a fuel line
and gas starts flooding in here

158
00:07:27,245 --> 00:07:29,934
I'm going to look really stupid.

